# 🟢 Level 1 – Beginner Explanation

# What is Wireless Networking?

A wireless network (Wi-Fi) allows devices to communicate **without cables** using radio waves.

Example:

```text
Laptop
      📶
      │
Wi-Fi Router
      │
Internet
```

Examples of Wi-Fi devices:

* Laptop
* Smartphone
* Smart TV
* Printer
* IoT Devices
* CCTV Cameras

---

# What is IEEE 802.11?

IEEE 802.11 is the family of standards that defines how Wi-Fi works.

| Standard              | Band        | Max Speed (Approx.)       |
| --------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------- |
| 802.11a               | 5 GHz       | 54 Mbps                   |
| 802.11b               | 2.4 GHz     | 11 Mbps                   |
| 802.11g               | 2.4 GHz     | 54 Mbps                   |
| 802.11n (Wi-Fi 4)     | 2.4/5 GHz   | Up to 600 Mbps            |
| 802.11ac (Wi-Fi 5)    | 5 GHz       | Multi-Gbps                |
| 802.11ax (Wi-Fi 6/6E) | 2.4/5/6 GHz | Higher efficiency & speed |

---

